### 错误标注
1. the lunar eighth month → the ninth day of the ninth lunar month（月份写错）
2. both number nine get together so call it ChongYang → two nines overlap, so it is called the Double Ninth Festival（语法错误、表达生硬）
3. In this day → On this day（介词固定搭配）
4. take costoms → follow customs（拼写错误；搭配错误）
5. get hight → climb mountains（拼写错误；中式英语）
6. Ju flowers → chrysanthemums
7. alcohols of Ju flower → chrysanthemum wine（alcohol 不可数，用词不当）
8. plant ZhuYu → wear dogwood（习俗是佩戴茱萸不是种植）
9. is carried with symbol of respecting elders → stands for respecting the elderly（carry 用词错误）
10. company → accompany（company 是名词）
11. respection → respect（无 respection 这个单词）
12. wish → best wishes（常用复数）
13. was carried with → embodies（时态、动词搭配错误）
14. pespecting → respecting（拼写错误）


### 美化版本
The Double Ninth Festival falls on the ninth day of the ninth lunar month. It is a time-honored traditional Chinese festival. Ancient people regarded nine as a yang number. 
Since two nines overlap, the festival is named the Double Ninth Festival. On this day, people follow customs including climbing mountains, appreciating chrysanthemums, drinking
chrysanthemum wine and wearing dogwood. Nowadays, the festival stands for respecting the elderly. Many people accompany their senior family members to show respect and best 
wishes. It embodies the traditional Chinese virtue of respecting the elderly.


### 标准参考译文
The Double Ninth Festival, a time-honored traditional Chinese festival, is celebrated on the ninth day of the ninth lunar month. The ancients considered nine a yang number. The
meeting of two nines gives the festival its name. Traditionally, people climb mountains, admire chrysanthemums, drink chrysanthemum wine and wear dogwood on this day. Today, 
it is associated with respecting the elderly. Many people stay with their elders to express respect and blessings. The festival represents the fine Chinese tradition of 
respecting senior citizens.


